Ours.  The ZZ9K-SOFT3D extension goes, and with it the server's probe of
ioctl 18 at every start.

- It served a 3D client's buffer swap through ZZ9KIOC_BLITX (ioctl 18), a
  call the 1.1 card driver does not have: that number is left unassigned
  because other builds of the driver use it, so the probe asked an
  unknown driver build to do whatever its 18 does;
- the soft3D client it served is not part of this system, and the
  request had no source bounds and no version request.

